d 'INDSAT': module to evaluate indicator saturation for outliers and structural breaks 
d
d   indsat is a library of indicator-saturation tools under one
d central command. It detects outliers, location shifts, trend
d breaks and coefficient breaks by general-to-specific selection
d over saturating sets of impulse (IIS), step (SIS), broken-trend
d (TIS, quadratic, cubic), differenced and pairwise impulse,
d multiplicative (MIS), designed (volcanic, transitory-change,
d ramp, user shape) and user-specified indicators, including super
d and ultra saturation and common break dates. The default search
d is a port of R gets::isat (Pretis, Reade and Sucarrat 2018) and
d reproduces its results numerically; the split-half estimators of
d Johansen and Nielsen (2009) and Nielsen and Qian (2025) and the
d m-step Huber-skip estimator (Johansen and Nielsen 2016) are also
d provided. Typed without variables after regress, newey or ardl,
d indsat saturates the model in memory and reports the breaks,
d outliers, dashboard graphs and a comparison of original and
d robust estimates (tables and coefficient graph). Subcommands
d cover ARDL / error-correction models with saturation and the
d Pesaran-Shin-Smith bounds test, results over a grid of target
d sizes with the Jiao-Pretis scaling tests, gauge theory, Monte
d Carlo gauge/potency, and postestimation (break dates and regimes,
d coefficient paths, isattest, outlier and distortion tests, bias
d correction, forecasting, diagnostics, dashboards). 
d
d KW: indicator saturation
d KW: outliers
d KW: structural breaks
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261112
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
